# nvfbc-relay policy replay fixture
# Avatar 60x2 in-game DLSS frame generation on the D3D11 flip-model present (b:vsync), -src 60 -lock -lag 75 -mark -etw -dejit, 2026-09-16: ONE benchmark test, no fade at either end, opened 2.3 s after the fade ends instead of the usual 0.3 s margin. First Avatar capture by the loop that skips grab-timeout re-deliveries, with the lock re-engage convergence window live. The field decided passthrough on every present. The later start is the replay model's requirement, not the field's: cut 0.3 s after the fade the model's cold-start convergence runs past the 200-present warmup and reports a 47-present blend run the field never had, while from 2.3 s on it tracks the field (0.1% against 0.0%). The benchmark is fully running by then, which is the window the fixture wants anyway. The window still covers 28 s of one steady test.
# units: microseconds. first value absolute, rest are deltas.
description Avatar 60x2 in-game DLSS frame generation on the D3D11 flip-model present (b:vsync), -src 60 -lock -lag 75 -mark -etw -dejit, 2026-09-16: ONE benchmark test, no fade at either end, opened 2.3 s after the fade ends instead of the usual 0.3 s margin. First Avatar capture by the loop that skips grab-timeout re-deliveries, with the lock re-engage convergence window live. The field decided passthrough on every present. The later start is the replay model's requirement, not the field's: cut 0.3 s after the fade the model's cold-start convergence runs past the 200-present warmup and reports a 47-present blend run the field never had, while from 2.3 s on it tracks the field (0.1% against 0.0%). The benchmark is fully running by then, which is the window the fixture wants anyway. The window still covers 28 s of one steady test.
# What the RELAY did on this capture. The replay model is only trustworthy
# for a configuration where it reproduces these; the test checks that.
field_worst_run 0
field_long_runs 0
field_synth_pct 0.0
src_hint 60.0
# Replay 0.1% / worst 1 against field 0.0% / worst 0 over 1686 presents. The happy-path gate on
# the shipping capture loop: the field passed every present of this window through sharp, so any
# change that blends here at all is visible immediately and the bound has almost no room in it.
# The model's single blend is its own cold-start tail, which is why this window opens 2.8 s after
# the fade rather than 0.3 s; see the description.
max_worst_run 1
max_long_runs 0
max_synth_pct 0.5
min_reseeds 0
